## ADR-DATA-001 — Atomic Transaction + Optimistic Concurrency

| Field | Content |
| --- | --- |
| **ID** | ADR-DATA-001 |
| **Status** | Decided — M2 |
| **Context** | Status changes must update `ServiceRequest` and write a `StatusHistory` row together (NFR004). Concurrent staff updates, whether status or assignment, must not cause silent data loss. |
| **Constraints** | CON003: small team, free tools, so the design must stay simple. CON005: the audit trail must be designed in from the start. |
| **Alternatives** | 1) Pessimistic row locking: rejected, because it blocks other staff while a request is being edited. 2) Last write wins: rejected, because it silently loses updates. 3) Commit status first and write the audit later via an outbox (A2 Approach B): rejected, because the audit could lag and it needs extra infrastructure. |
| **Decision** | Wrap every status change and assignment in one transaction. Add a `version` integer to `ServiceRequest` that covers every write to it. Update with `WHERE id = ? AND version = ?`. Order: guard → conditional update → row check → audit observer → commit → notification. If zero rows are updated, roll back and return a conflict error. The audit observer does not run. |
| **Trade-offs** | Each update carries a small version-check overhead. Conflict errors must be handled in the UI. This is accepted because updates are infrequent and NFR004 correctness matters more than write speed. |
| **Risks** | Staff may see conflict errors on busy requests. Mitigation: a clear "reload and try again" message. A new code path could write to `ServiceRequest` without the version check. Mitigation: all writes go through `ServiceRequestService`, and PR review checks for it. |
| **Evidence** | A2 Task 2 (5.2–5.3): EdPrice-MSFT (2023a) on transactions; Databricks Staff (2026) on optimistic concurrency; Amazon Web Services (2025) on the outbox; OWASP (2019) on server-side validation. NFR004: history not editable or deletable by normal users. |
| **Later consequence** | Update at M3 with a concurrency test: two parallel updates on one request. One must fail with a conflict, and no extra `StatusHistory` row may appear. |
| **RTM link** | RTM-008 (FR008); RTM-009 (FR009); RTM-011 (FR011); RTM-017 (NFR004) |
